# API server port (the dev script already sets 4001)
PORT=4001

# Comma-separated list of origins allowed by CORS
ALLOWED_API_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4000

# Auth: one env-backed dummy user, no table (docs/features/auth.md).
# DEV=TRUE skips credentials entirely — every request is authenticated and the
# login screen forwards straight to the app. Set DEV=FALSE (or remove it) to
# require the email + password below on the login screen.
DEV=TRUE
AUTH_EMAIL=demo@reclit.app
AUTH_PASSWORD=change-me
# Optional key for signing the session cookie; defaults to the pair above.
# AUTH_SECRET=

# Postgres connection string used by Prisma (see prisma.config.ts).
# Supabase: use the "Session pooler" string from Project Settings → Database —
# the direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host is IPv6-only.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/app

# Supabase Storage for POST /files uploads into the public bucket "reclit".
# The publishable (anon) key works when the bucket allows anon inserts; if its
# RLS rejects them, put the service-role key in this same variable instead.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_KEY=

# Trigger.dev background jobs (apps/api/trigger.config.ts). Dev key from the
# Trigger.dev dashboard -> project -> API keys. The api needs it to enqueue
# `run-ai-batch` jobs (`runAi.runCells` answers BAD_GATEWAY without it).
# `bun run trigger:dev` loads this file, so the local worker also gets
# DATABASE_URL, the AI key and the ElevenLabs key; a deployed Trigger
# environment needs them set in its own dashboard.
TRIGGER_SECRET_KEY=

# The AI provider's key, used through the Vercel AI SDK (src/ai/model.ts — the
# one file that knows which provider it is); the `google_search` node's
# grounding runs on the same key. Used by the Trigger.dev worker (cells, the
# assistant's tool loop, the dashboard generation's brief / cards / review
# calls) and by the api for the onboarding's describe and suggest calls; the
# api also checks it before starting a dashboard generation
# (dashboardGeneration.start answers SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE without it). The
# provider SDK's own variable name is still read as a fallback.
AI_API_KEY=

# The model every AI call uses. Optional; defaults to the provider's default
# in src/ai/model.ts.
# AI_MODEL=

# ElevenLabs key for Speech-to-Text (src/ai/elevenlabs.ts): the header
# capsule's mic recording is transcribed through POST /assistant/transcribe
# (the api; without it the route answers 503 and the capsule hides the mic
# result). Audio CELLS are not sent here: the worker converts them, like every
# file, with markitdown (Python, no key) — the local interpreter is
# apps/api/.venv; see docs/features/external-api.md "Local setup".
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# A stronger model for the assistant's tool-calling loop and the dashboard
# generation's calls (the worker) (src/ai/assistant-step.ts). Optional;
# defaults to AI_MODEL.
# ASSISTANT_MODEL=

# Firecrawl key for the `crawl-website` task (src/ai/firecrawl.ts): a url cell
# in an AI node's row is crawled once (25 pages, subdomains included), the
# pages cached in the ExternalApi table and reused from any cell holding the
# same URL. The worker also crawls the company profile's website
# (`crawl-company`), and the api scrapes its homepage in company.setWebsite
# (COMPANY_AI_UNAVAILABLE without this key or the AI key). Without it a
# cell run still completes and the prompt says the site could not be crawled.
# Get one at firecrawl.dev -> API Keys.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Resend key for the Mail (`email`) node (src/ai/resend.ts): a mail cell drafts
# an email with the model and sends it to one of its row's email cells. Used by
# the Trigger.dev worker, not the api; without it a mail cell fails with the
# reason. The sender domain must be verified in Resend -> Domains. Get one at
# resend.com -> API Keys.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# The sender. Optional; defaults to "Reclit <hello@reclit.com>". Avoid
# no-reply addresses — one-way senders score worse with spam filters.
# RESEND_FROM=Reclit <hello@reclit.com>
